  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...1) Dry weather with gradually increasing temperatures\nthrough the end of the week under high pressure.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure ridge axis will settle over the state tonight, \nand calmer winds are in store for the rest of the week.\n\nTemperatures will gradually increase, settling out in the 80s \nSaturday and Sunday. Clear skies and calm winds tonight will allow \nfor effective radiational cooling, and lows could dip to around 50 \nDowneast, and into the upper 40s across the north. This may lead to \npatchy river valley fog over the area tonight and again Friday \nnight. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for a system moving in early next \nweek, bringing another round of wetting rainfall.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure lingers over the region this weekend, as low \npressure east of the Carolinas moves northeast into the Gulf of \nMaine by Monday. To the north, another low pressure over Canada\nmoves towards the region as well. Wetting rainfall expected, \nwith higher totals along Downeast. There could be a chance of \nthunderstorms along the frontal boundary of another low pressure\nsystem moving in Tuesday.",
